==Battleground==
*30 [[Snache]]s spawn after 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*10 [[Those Guys]] spawn after 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>, delay 3.33~13.33 seconds<sup>100f~400f</sup>.
*10 [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn after 5 seconds<sup>150f</sup>, delay 4~20 seconds<sup>120f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 6.67~16.67 seconds<sup>200f~500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>, delay 10~23.33 seconds<sup>300f~700f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>, delay 36.67 seconds<sup>1,100f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Dancer Cat (Enemy)|Dancer Cat]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn, delay 13.33~26.67 seconds<sup>400f~800f</sup>.
**10 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn, delay 36.67~43.33 seconds<sup>1,100f~1,300f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage is a battle of attrition, as most peons should pose little threat in any situation, leaving a one versus one against the boss. Due to Dancer Cat's high range and fast attack rate, you will want to bring rushers like [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]], [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Butterfly/Fishman Cat]], [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], among other [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|Anti-Traitless Cats]] you may own at this point. [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]] only barely outrange the boss, and can serve as good supplemental damage if you can ensure Dancer Cat doesn't push throughout the battle. Three meatshields is the optimal amount to prevent most enemies from gaining ground here.

You can bring the [[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper Cat]] Battle Item to let you better control the enemies on field, [[Battle Items#Rich Cat|Rich Cat]] is unnecessary as you can farm the opening enemies for cash before engaging the boss. If you can spare some slots in your lineup, bringing any Attack Up [[Cat Combo]] will help expedite this stage immensely.

